reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:30:        "hypothesis": "An authenticated administrator at cartflows_manage_settings privilege can supply a path-traversal sequence (e.g. '../../../../wp-config.php') in the $_REQUEST['handle'] parameter to delete arbitrary files outside CARTFLOWS_LOG_DIR.",
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:31:        "trace": "user_actions() [line 71] ← called on admin page load ← cartflows_manage_settings capability check [line 76] ← $button_action == 'remove-log' ← delete_log_file() [line 87] ← $file_name = trim(sanitize_text_field($_REQUEST['handle'])) [line 183] → $file_path = CARTFLOWS_LOG_DIR . $file_name [line 184] → wp_delete_file($file_path) [line 187]",
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:32:        "defenses_analyzed": "Nonce check at lines 173-177 (wp_verify_nonce 'remove_log'). Capability check: cartflows_manage_settings at user_actions() line 76. sanitize_text_field() does NOT strip '../'. No realpath() containment. No extension allowlist in delete_log_file(). Contrast: the AJAX download_cf_log() in admin-core/ajax/debugger.php does use realpath() at line 212-215 for the same operation.",
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:44:            "result": "REFUTED for meaningful severity — requires cartflows_manage_settings capability, which is granted only to the 'administrator' role (admin-menu.php:339-350). In WordPress security model, administrators are considered trusted and have other means of file system access."
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:73:        "hypothesis": "An authenticated administrator at cartflows_manage_settings privilege can supply a path-traversal sequence in $_REQUEST['handle'] to read arbitrary .log files outside CARTFLOWS_LOG_DIR.",
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:74:        "trace": "user_actions() [line 71] ← cartflows_manage_settings capability check [line 76] ← $button_action == 'download-log' ← download_log_file() [line 91] ← nonce check 'download_log' [line 197] ← $file_name = trim(sanitize_text_field($_REQUEST['handle'])) [line 203] → $file_path = CARTFLOWS_LOG_DIR . $file_name [line 204] → file_get_contents($file_path) [line 224] → echo output",
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:75:        "defenses_analyzed": "Nonce check at lines 197-201. Capability check: cartflows_manage_settings at line 76. Extension check: only '.log' allowed (line 214). '.php' substring blocked (line 214). No realpath() containment (inconsistency with AJAX version in debugger.php). sanitize_text_field() does not strip '../'.",
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:87:            "result": "REFUTED for meaningful severity — requires cartflows_manage_settings (administrator role only)."
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:100:      "area": "IR anom_1: Missing nonce — wp_ajax_cartflows_dismiss_script_migration_complete_notice",
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:102:      "reason": "dismiss_script_migration_complete_notice() at class-cartflows-admin-notices.php:418 has current_user_can('manage_options') at line 420 and check_ajax_referer('cartflows-dismiss-script-migration-complete-notice','security') at line 424. The capability check uses wp_send_json_error() which calls die(). No side-effect precedes nonce verification."
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:107:      "reason": "json_search_flows() at class-cartflows-wd-flow-product-meta.php:83 has cartflows_manage_flows_steps capability check at line 85 (returns error on failure) and wp_verify_nonce check at line 89 (inside if-block). SQL uses $wpdb->prepare() with $wpdb->esc_like(). IR claim of 'side-effect at line 86' is incorrect — wp_send_json_error() is an error response, not a persistent state change."
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:112:      "reason": "upload_checkout_file() at class-cartflows-checkout-ajax.php:293 checks check_ajax_referer('wcf-file-upload','security',false) at line 295 and sends JSON error on failure (effectively terminates). Nonce is generated in checkout page JS vars (class-cartflows-checkout-markup.php:1776) accessible to guest checkout users. File type is validated by allowlist (jpg/jpeg/png/gif/webp/ico/pdf/mp3/m4a/wav/mp4/m4v/mov), wp_check_filetype_and_ext(), filename randomized with UUID. No executable files can be uploaded. The nopriv hook is by-design for guest checkout with file upload."
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:115:      "area": "IR anom_4: Missing capability — wp_ajax_cartflows_save_tutor_course_template",
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:117:      "reason": "ajax_save_course_template() at tutor-lms/class-cartflows-tutor-compatibility.php:198 has wp_verify_nonce (NONCE_NAME='cartflows_tutor_template_save') at line 201 and current_user_can('edit_post', $course_id) at line 217. Both checks are present and correct. IR was incorrect in flagging as missing."
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:125:      "area": "IR anom_6/36: Flawed nonce / inconsistency — wp_ajax_cartflows_snooze_script_migration",
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:127:      "reason": "snooze_script_migration_notice() at class-cartflows-admin-notices.php:177 has check_ajax_referer('cartflows-snooze-script-migration','security',false) at line 179 (sends JSON error on failure) and current_user_can('manage_options') at line 183. The $die=false pattern with immediate wp_send_json_error() response is functionally equivalent to $die=true. No state mutation precedes the nonce check."
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:135:      "area": "IR anom_8: Flawed nonce — wp_ajax_cartflows_get_suretriggers_data",
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:137:      "reason": "get_suretriggers_data() at class-cartflows-suretriggers-compatibility.php:115 has current_user_can('cartflows_manage_settings') at line 120 and check_ajax_referer at line 127. The '$die=false' with wp_send_json_error() is safe. No state mutation precedes checks."
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:152:      "reason": "order_detail_form_shortcode() at class-cartflows-init-blocks.php:141 has check_ajax_referer('wpcf_ajax_nonce','nonce') at line 143 (TOP of function, before any side-effects) and cartflows_manage_flows_steps check at line 145. The additional nonce checks at lines 161 and 175 are inside filter callbacks registered for do_shortcode() — they are redundant re-verifications, not primary guards. The primary guard at line 143 executes before any state changes."
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:157:      "reason": "apply_coupon() at class-cartflows-checkout-ajax.php:106 has check_ajax_referer('wcf-apply-coupon','security',false) at line 109, sends JSON error on failure. No capability check is expected or needed for a public checkout coupon action. coupon_code is sanitized with sanitize_text_field(). WooCommerce cart handles coupon validation internally."
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:162:      "reason": "Shortcode/block attributes flow into post meta fields stored via save_meta_fields() with appropriate FILTER_SANITIZE_STRING, FILTER_WP_KSES, or FILTER_WP_KSES_POST sanitizers. Custom CSS/JS fields use FILTER_SCRIPT which encodes with htmlentities() at save and decodes at output — by design for admin-configurable code injection. This requires cartflows_manage_flows_steps or cartflows_manage_settings capability to set. Verified in meta-ops.php:95-99."
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:170:      "area": "IR anom_37: Inconsistency — wp_ajax_cartflows_install_plugin",
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:172:      "reason": "add_action('wp_ajax_cartflows_install_plugin', 'wp_ajax_install_plugin') delegates to WordPress core's wp_ajax_install_plugin() function (admin-ajax.php), which has its own nonce check ('install-plugin') and install_plugins capability check. The plugin is providing a custom action name that safely delegates to the audited WordPress core handler."
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:177:      "reason": "Every REST route in admin-core/api/ (flows.php, flow-data.php, step-data.php, common-settings.php, home-page.php, learn.php, product/product-data.php, webhooks.php) has 'permission_callback' set to a class method (get_items_permissions_check, permissions_check, etc.) that performs current_user_can() checks requiring cartflows_manage_flows_steps or cartflows_manage_settings. The semgrep rule triggered on the IR's __array_callable__ placeholder, not the actual code."
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:185:      "area": "Semgrep wp-xss-echo-no-escape — class-cartflows-functions.php:292",
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:190:      "area": "Semgrep wp-xss-stored-option-meta — class-cartflows-frontend.php:545,551,557,574,580",
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:192:      "reason": "These lines output custom CSS and JS stored in get_option('_cartflows_global_scripts') and get_post_meta(flow_id, 'wcf-flow-custom-css/js'). These fields are: (1) saved only by users with cartflows_manage_settings capability; (2) intentionally unescaped because they contain raw CSS/JS to be injected into <style>/<script> tags. This is by-design admin code injection, not exploitable XSS."
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:197:      "reason": "show_cf_log() at debugger.php:102 has cartflows_manage_settings capability check at line 104 and check_ajax_referer at line 108. $log_filename is set to $logs[$log_key] (array lookup against filesystem-scanned log files), not directly from user input. The path cannot traverse outside CARTFLOWS_LOG_DIR via this lookup."
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:207:      "reason": "Requires cartflows_manage_settings (administrator only). The technical path traversal exists but is not exploitable below admin privilege level."
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:212:      "reason": "The update_option() calls in importer.php use hardcoded option keys ('_cartflows_store_checkout', '_cartflows_common') — no user-controlled option key. The function requires cartflows_manage_flows_steps capability and nonce. The semgrep pattern flagged the option write but the key is not user-controlled."
reports/phase2/cartflows-phase2.claude.raw.json:217:      "reason": "The $target_url in user_onboarding() at line 196 is hardcoded: CARTFLOWS_TEMPLATES_URL . 'wp-json/cartflows-server/v1/add-subscriber'. It is a constant concatenation, not user input. Function requires manage_options and nonce."
